 adjusted for a 1:1 bonus issue in Nov 2025.\n- Consolidated Debt/Equity stood at 1.63x; credit ratings are ICRA A1+ (short term) and ICRA A / CRISIL A (Stable) for long term, reflecting the group's leveraged NBFC-cum-broking balance sheet.\n- Future outlook emphasises a shift toward fee-based income alongside continued reinvestment in technology and distribution.","src":"deck","title":"Capital allocation policy (investor deck)"}],"business":[{"body":"- Transformed from a pure broking firm into a diversified financial-services powerhouse covering Broking/Distribution/Trading, Financing (NBFC) and Insurance Broking, plus PMS, wealth management, investment banking, arbitrage/HFT prop trading, discount broking (StoxKart) and GIFT City IFSC operations.\n- Strategic alliances with 8 PSU and private banks (PNB, UBI, CBI, IOB, Ujjivan, etc.) offering online trading, including 3-in-1 bank+demat+trading tie-ups, and clearing-member status across all major exchanges.\n- Established national brand with deep penetration and corporate relationships across trading members, authorised persons and financial distributors.","src":"deck","title":"Positioning (investor deck)"},{"body":"- [Corporate structure] The group operates through multiple wholly/majority-owned subsidiaries: Moneywise Financial Services (NBFC, 100%), SMC Investech (formerly SMC Real Estate Advisors, unlisted share trading, 100%), SMC Capitals (Category-1 Merchant Banker, 100%), SMC Global IFSC (100%), Pulin Comtrade (commodity trading, 100%), SMC Comex International DMCC-UAE (proprietary trading, 100%), SMC Insurance Brokers (90%), StoxKart Fintech (formerly Moneywise Finvest, discount brokerage, 100%), and SMC Investments & Advisors (advisory, 100%).\n- [Leadership/promoters] Founded in 1994 by Mr. Subhash C. Aggarwal (Chairman & Managing Director) and Mr. Mahesh C. Gupta (Vice Chairman & Managing Director); management team includes multiple family members (Aggarwal/Gupta) heading group entities, plus a professio